 ## Overview
-IRON is a neural inverse rendering pipeline that reconstructs high-quality 3D triangle meshes and spatially varying material textures from photometric images captured with a collocated flashlight and moving camera [S1]. It distinguishes itself from standard NeRF-based methods by outputting explicit mesh-compatible representations (SDFs and material maps) rather than implicit radiance fields, and from direct mesh optimization methods by employing a hybrid two-stage training scheme that first recovers correct topology via volumetric rendering before refining geometry with edge-aware surface rendering [S1].
+IRON is a neural inverse rendering pipeline that reconstructs high-quality 3D triangle meshes and spatially varying material textures from photometric images captured with a collocated flashlight and moving camera [S1]. It solves the problem of jointly optimizing geometry and appearance by using a hybrid optimization scheme: it first recovers correct object topology using volumetric radiance field rendering, then refines geometry and disentangles materials from lighting using edge-aware physics-based surface rendering [S1]. This approach distinguishes IRON from methods that optimize surface rendering directly, which often diverge or get stuck in local minima with incorrect topology [S1].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** A set of photometric images. These are captured assuming opaque objects, no ambient light, and a flashlight co-located with the camera. Shadows and global illumination effects (interreflections) are ignored [S1].
-*   **Output:** A triangle mesh and material textures (diffuse albedo, specular albedo, roughness) derived from the optimized neural networks [S1].
+*   **Input:** A set of photometric images captured with a flashlight co-located with the camera. Assumptions: opaque objects, no ambient light, shadows and global illumination (interreflections) are ignored [S1].
+*   **Output:** A triangle mesh and material textures (diffuse albedo, specular albedo, roughness) [S1].
 
